{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/bznew8","slideIndex":6,"text":"Use binary edge variables with flow-conservation penalties. Start with a small graph and verify the QUBO optimum against an exact classical solution. Flow conservation can allow disconnected cycles, so explicitly detect or constrain those. Run shallow QAOA on Qiskit Aer, validate the samples and retain only feasible results. Compare identical costs, graph and constraints. Simulator experiments alone do not establish quantum advantage.\n\nProject sources: README.md; QuantumRescue_Implementation_Plan.md. Repository snapshot reviewed 1 November 2026."}
